mn13:7.6 starts: Odours cognizable by the nose
mn13:7.7 starts: Flavours cognizable by the tongue
mn13:7.8 starts: Tangibles cognizable by the body that are wished for,
mn13:23-28.3 starts: disconnected bones scattered in all directions—here a hand-bone,
mn13:29.2 starts: bones bleached white, the colour of shells
mn13:33-35.2 starts: With the fading away as well of rapture
mn13:33-35.3 starts: With the abandoning of pleasure and pain he enters
an8.46:1.3 starts: when a number of agreeable-bodied deities approached him,
an8.46:6.1 starts: “Here, Bhante, I had gone off to pass the day
